.TH ROOZ 1 "October 2026" "Roozlet 0.4.0"
.SH NAME
rooz \- compact offline Persian calendar for Xfce
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rooz
[--widget | --calendar | --search | --personal | --settings | --reset-position | --quit | --check-data | --version]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rooz is a single-instance desktop date card. Double-click opens the month view.
The default civil timezone is Asia/Tehran. Interface language and digits are independent.
Official occasions and Iranian Hijri mapping are bundled for Solar Hijri year 1405 only.
Other years show explicit missing-coverage messages.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --widget
Start or retain the compact card only. Intended for user login startup.
.TP
.B --calendar
Open or raise the existing month window.
.TP
.B --settings
Open bilingual preferences.
.TP
.B --search
Open offline date, occasion and personal-entry search. Ctrl+F in the calendar also opens search.
.TP
.B --personal
Open notes and reminders. Ctrl+N in the calendar adds an entry to the selected day.
.TP
.B --reset-position
Return the card to the primary monitor's upper-right work area.
.TP
.B --quit
Gracefully quit the existing app.
.TP
.B --check-data
Validate and report annual data without a graphical display.
.TP
.B --version
Print the app version without a graphical display.
.SH FILES
XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rooz/config.json; XDG_DATA_HOME/rooz/calendars/; XDG_DATA_HOME/rooz/personal.sqlite3; XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/rooz.desktop
.SH NOTES
Login startup is opt-in. No network requests or privileged background service are used.
Desktop notifications are off by default. Enable them in Desktop & startup settings
or Notes & reminders, then select notification for each entry.
Reminders are checked every 30 seconds while Roozlet runs; startup and resume catch
missed occurrences from the preceding 24 hours. Delivery depends on the desktop service.
Entries may repeat daily, weekly, or annually in the Shamsi calendar.
Esfand 30 anniversaries use Esfand's last day in non-leap years.
Completion applies to the selected occurrence. Delete is reversible with Undo.
User notes are stored locally with owner-only filesystem permissions and preserved on upgrade.
